# Logo master artwork — large source files, kept outside version control.
# NOTE the five SVGs under logo/SVG/ are already TRACKED and stay so: they are
# the only remaining record of funky's logo inks (#E1F708, #F6F4F1, #D9DB00),
# which is what made deleting the unreferenced funky assets from public/ safe.
/logo/
/logo.zip

# Local `<name>.bak-<date>` copies, made before editing a config file. These
# were sitting un-ignored in the working tree, where a `git add -A` would have
# staged them.
*.bak-*

# Private source material at the repo root — résumés, portfolio, drafts
/*.pdf
/portfolio/
/intro.txt
content/posts/*.txt

# Local agent/planning tool output
/.lavish/

# Local MCP client config — machine-specific endpoints and request headers,
# so it belongs to the environment rather than the repo. Keep it local.
/claude_desktop_config.json


# NOTE the three *_dark-mono.svg marks under public/ are deliberately TRACKED,
# and the *_light-primary marks with them.
#
# Corrected 2026-10-26. This used to say ThemedLogo serves the dark-mono files
# and that ignoring them "ships a site with no logo". That stopped being true at
# the 2026-10-17 mask unification: ThemedLogo now stencils ONLY the three
# *_light-primary.svg files (one masked span per role, in every theme), so those
# are the build-critical ones. Of the dark-mono set, only
# ttt_icon_dark-mono.svg is still referenced — layout.tsx's static icon /
# shortcut / apple-touch-icon and DEFAULT_URL in lib/palette/favicon.ts.
# ttt_horizontal_dark-mono.svg and ttt_stacked-tagline_dark-mono.svg are
# referenced by nothing and stay anyway: CLAUDE.md note 7 keeps them as the
# record of what the mark's ink is supposed to be, which is the evidence behind
# the single masked mark's one condition.
